# Trivy vulnerability exception file for cicd-devsecops-demo.
#
# Policy (docs/adr and research.md D5): the pipeline blocks promotion ONLY on
# CRITICAL/HIGH findings that have a known fix available (`--ignore-unfixed`). A CVE
# with no fix available can never appear here as a "workaround" — it already doesn't
# block, by policy, so it needs no entry. This file exists ONLY for a reviewed,
# time-boxed exception to a *fixable* HIGH/CRITICAL finding that the team has
# deliberately decided not to fix yet (e.g. the fix is not yet compatible with our base
# image, or is scheduled for the next release).
#
# Format: one CVE id per line, followed by a comment with:
#   - who reviewed/approved the exception and when
#   - why the fix is deferred
#   - a re-review date (exceptions are not permanent)
#
# Example (remove once a real exception is needed):
# CVE-2024-00000 # reviewed 2026-09-22 by @maintainer — fix requires base image bump
#                # scheduled for next release; re-review by 2026-10-22
#
# No exceptions are currently in effect.
